---
import PlatformLayout from "../../layouts/PlatformLayout.astro";
export const prerender = true;
---
<PlatformLayout title="Engine and Editor" description="Explore implemented Kéire Engine, Editor, Hub, rendering, scripting, VFX, and content-pipeline capabilities." active="product">
    <section class="platform-section"><div class="platform-shell">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Engine + Editor · Kéire 0.4.1</p><h1>Production-minded systems with visible contracts.</h1></div><p>Kéire 0.4.1 is the current checked-in release. Download links remain catalog-controlled: this website shows a package only after its signed catalog entry is active, without substituting local release-candidate artifacts.</p></div>
        <div class="editorial-grid">
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">01</span><h3>Scenes, prefabs, and Play Mode</h3><p>Typed components, nested prefab overrides, tags, transactional edits, deterministic serialization, and shared Editor/player multi-scene worlds.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">02</span><h3>Shader and Material Graphs</h3><p>Reusable functions and layers, explicit transparency modes, live previews, world-scoped parameter collections, and managed material-slot instances.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">03</span><h3>VFX and deterministic replay</h3><p>CPU/GPU graphs, events, strips, mesh and volume output, diagnostics, bounded pools, and versioned runtime checkpoints.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">04</span><h3>C# gameplay services</h3><p>Reload-safe behaviours, multi-scene queries, physics casts, input rebinding, runtime UI, render controls, and typed native-asset residency.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">05</span><h3>Animation and procedural motion</h3><p>Graph playback, retargeting, semantic rigs, IK, terrain-aware contacts, procedural humanoid locomotion, and presentation interpolation.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">06</span><h3>Deterministic asset pipeline</h3><p>Isolated import, targeted dependency-closure refresh, stable identities, transactional publication, hardened archives, and reproducible cooking.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">07</span><h3>Hub and player delivery</h3><p>Independent Editor installations, project and package tasks, Build Support, signed catalogs, and published Windows, DEB, and RPM artifacts.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">08</span><h3>Observable failure boundaries</h3><p>Structured diagnostics, last-good runtime state, recovery journals, profiler evidence, bounded queues, and explicit release gates.</p></article>
            <article class="editorial-panel"><span class="editorial-panel__index">09</span><h3>Dense-scene performance</h3><p>The profiled Distribution Showcase moved from 30.83 ms to 4.99 ms average frame time while draw calls fell from 1,390 to 61 and steady-state dynamic-buffer reallocations reached zero.</p></article>
        </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="platform-section platform-section--line"><div class="platform-shell cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Evidence, not slogans</p><h2>Read the architecture and release gates.</h2></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/reference/overview/">Architecture overview</a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/docs/reference/production-readiness-review/">Readiness review</a></div></div></section>
</PlatformLayout>
